1. Have more realistic weight listings and abilities. Carrying two types
of armor and even more sets of weapons gets a little ridiculous

2. Have lots more ways to have magic items either lost or destroyed at the
higher levels. Unique artifacts might be immune, but it makes life that
more interesting if an adventurer can lose their inventory. How about
teleporters that move one sans all one's equipment?

3. On a less evil note, how about a level where all magic simply doesn't
function? Magical bonuses disappear, wands fail, and so forth.

I have other ideas for what I'd like to see in a nethack game, but most
of them involve getting rid of hit points for something more realistic,
shifting over to a skill-based system, and trashing character classes.
But that's just me...

